  "label": "Exaggerated reaction trope",
  "description": "A common visual and narrative device in comedy and film where characters react with extreme emotion (e.g., wide eyes, open mouths) to something that is actually mundane or not particularly shocking. This trope is used here to create a humorous contrast between the intensity of the reaction and the triviality of the 'stupid post' being referenced.",
